      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that after reading 6 bytes from an 11-character ASCII string wrapped in a `ReaderInputStream`, exactly 5 bytes remain available in the encoder's output buffer. Let me write an improved version with clearer names and structure.Now I'll run the compile check.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version replaces cryptic auto-generated variable names (`stringReader0`, `int0`, etc.) with descriptive ones (`sourceReader`, `bytesRead`, `bytesRemainingInBuffer`) and extracts magic numbers into named constants that explain the 11-character source, 6-byte read, and the expected 5 remaining bytes."
